From: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
Subject: [PATCH] nss_freq: no instruction counts while frequency scaling is off

With frequency scaling off (dev.nss.clock.auto_scale=0, or a pinned
dev.nss.clock.current_freq) the firmware still reported its instruction
count every millisecond: 1000 of the 1700 status messages a second an
idle IPQ5018 AP received, and more than half of its NSS interrupts, only
to keep cpu_load_ubi current. Stop the counts at the current frequency
in both paths; cpu_load_ubi then holds its last value. initialized still
keeps samples that arrive late from turning scaling back on.

Measured on IPQ5018 (switching the counts at runtime): status messages
1702/s -> 702/s, nss_queue0 interrupts 1064/s -> 468/s.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
---
--- a/nss_init.c
+++ b/nss_init.c
@@ -240,7 +240,7 @@
 	}
 	INIT_WORK((struct work_struct *)nss_work, nss_hal_wq_function);
 	nss_work->frequency = nss_cmd_buf.current_freq;
-	nss_work->stats_enable = 1;
+	nss_work->stats_enable = 0;
 
 	/*
 	 * Ensure we start with a fresh set of samples later
@@ -268,10 +268,22 @@
 
 	if (nss_cmd_buf.auto_scale != 1) {
 		/*
-		 * The instruction counts stay on, since the CPU load is computed
-		 * from them; initialized stops them from turning scaling back on.
+		 * With scaling off the firmware's instruction counts, a status
+		 * message every millisecond, only feed cpu_load_ubi: stop them at
+		 * the current frequency. initialized keeps late samples from
+		 * turning scaling back on.
 		 */
 		nss_runtime_samples.initialized = 1;
+		nss_runtime_samples.freq_scale_ready = 0;
+		nss_work = (nss_work_t *)kmalloc(sizeof(nss_work_t), GFP_ATOMIC);
+		if (!nss_work) {
+			nss_info("NSS Freq WQ kmalloc fail");
+			return ret;
+		}
+		INIT_WORK((struct work_struct *)nss_work, nss_hal_wq_function);
+		nss_work->frequency = nss_runtime_samples.freq_scale[nss_runtime_samples.freq_scale_index].frequency;
+		nss_work->stats_enable = 0;
+		queue_work(nss_wq, (struct work_struct *)nss_work);
 		return ret;
 	}
 
